From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-25)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: built-in AMFI, and the root-auth panic that would have eaten the first boot

Two things, and the second one is the reason this is not simply "enable another
driver".

**1. The root-auth panic.** bsd_init.c calls FSIOC_KERNEL_ROOTAUTH on the
mounted root and, for anything that is not macOS, sets require_rootauth = TRUE
and panics "rootvp not authenticated after mounting" if the volume will not
attest. The sweet port carries a widened branch that prints a line and
continues, because its HFS root cannot be a sealed volume - there is no
rootsnap, no chain of trust, and the kernel itself is booted unsigned. That
branch is inside #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET). So the first milanf
boot that actually mounts a root filesystem would have gone: UFS comes up from
0089, GPT is scanned, HFS mounts, FSIOC_KERNEL_ROOTAUTH fails, panic - and the
report would have said "rootvp not authenticated", which is true, expected, and
completely uninformative. Widened here alongside the AMFI work because it is
the same statement: this board has no chain of trust to extend.

**2. AMFI is load-bearing, not polish.** The 'amfi' interface pointer
(libkern/amfi/amfi.c) is NULL until something registers one, and on milanf
nothing does, because bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c is gated on
ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET and bsd_init.c never calls
sweet_amfi_policy_register(). What that means in practice:

  - kern_cs.c:739 has an explicit
    panic("CoreEntitlements: missing AMFI bridge") on amfi == NULL.
  - kern_trustcache.c:86 has panic("amfi interface not available"), and
    kern_trustcache.c:816 dereferences amfi->TrustCache.version with no NULL
    check at all. Both are behind a trust_cache_rt != NULL check that is
    probably false on a non-Apple boot, which is why milanf has not fallen over
    yet - but "probably" is doing a lot of work in that sentence.

  - The interesting loss is quieter. sweet_amfi.c's MAC policy is what sets
    CS_SIGNED and CS_PLATFORM_BINARY on every binary on the root filesystem
    (they are ad-hoc signed and would otherwise be platform binaries only
    through Apple's static trust cache, which does not exist here), and what
    attaches the XML entitlements blob to each signature. Without it, exec
    still works but every process is unentitled and unplatformed.

  - It also registers the "Sandbox" MAC policy. The port's own comment records
    what its absence costs: libsystem_sandbox calls __mac_syscall("Sandbox",
    ...) and without a policy of that name every call returns ENOPOLICY, at
    which point launchd reports "error = 159: Sandbox restriction", backboardd
    cannot reach mobilegestalt or iohideventsystem, and tccd says "profile not
    found". That is a userspace that looks like it is dying of a dozen
    unrelated diseases.

SweetEntitlements.cpp comes with it because it is the other half of one
mechanism: sweet_amfi.c declares its seven sweet_entitlements_* entry points as
extern, and this is the file that defines them. Enabling either alone would
leave a dangling reference - which is exactly what the linker would have said,
so at least that failure mode is loud.

Registration order is unchanged from sweet: the interface registers from
STARTUP(EARLY_BOOT, STARTUP_RANK_MIDDLE) so it exists before any exec, and the
two MAC policies register from bsd_init after vfsinit(), which is the first
point mac_policy_register() is legal.

IOLog/printf strings keep the SWEET: prefix, same reason as 0088/0089: the
pull and symbolication tooling greps them. The two prose comments that claimed
the board specifically are made board-neutral.

Verified without a compiler: apply --check exit 0 alone and in series order
behind 0086-0089 (none of those touch these three files), then a real apply to
a scratch tree - all cleanly, CR=0 in sources and patch. Link unverified; CI
in the morning.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index bb2a2bf..fbdfcd6 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -691,8 +691,8 @@ bsd_init(void)
 	bsd_init_kprintf("calling vfsinit\n");
 	vfsinit();
 
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
-	/* AMFI's MAC policy is built in on SWEET (bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c). */
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
+	/* AMFI and Sandbox MAC policies are built in (bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c). */
 	extern void sweet_amfi_policy_register(void);
 	sweet_amfi_policy_register();
 #endif
@@ -933,11 +933,12 @@ bsd_init(void)
 		if (require_rootauth) {
 			/* enforce sealedness */
 			int autherr = VNOP_IOCTL(rootvnode, FSIOC_KERNEL_ROOTAUTH, NULL, 0, vfs_context_kernel());
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 			/*
-			 * SWEET has no chain of trust to extend: the kernel itself is
-			 * booted unsigned and there is no Image4/AMFI, and its HFS root
-			 * cannot be a sealed volume. Report it instead of panicking.
+			 * This port has no chain of trust to extend: the kernel itself
+			 * is booted unsigned, there is no Image4 and no static trust
+			 * cache, and its HFS root cannot be a sealed volume. Report it
+			 * instead of panicking.
 			 */
 			if (autherr) {
 				printf("SWEET: root volume is not authenticated (error %d); continuing unsealed\n", autherr);
diff --git a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
index cb67b4d..a9f2fd4 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
  * Interfaces no kernel path uses on SWEET (they serve other Apple kexts)
  * panic with a clear message instead of being NULL.
  */
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 #include <kern/debug.h>
 #include <kern/startup.h>
 #include <libkern/amfi/amfi.h>
@@ -380,4 +380,4 @@ sweet_amfi_policy_register(void)
 	printf("SWEET Sandbox: permissive policy %s (%d)\n",
 	    error ? "NOT registered" : "registered", error);
 }
-#endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
+#endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET || ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF */
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetEntitlements.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetEntitlements.cpp
index 6186541..7310151 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetEntitlements.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetEntitlements.cpp
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
  */
 #include <pexpert/arm64/board_config.h>
 
-#if defined(SWEET)
+#if defined(SWEET) || defined(MILANF)
 #include <IOKit/IOLib.h>
 #include <libkern/c++/OSArray.h>
 #include <libkern/c++/OSBoolean.h>
@@ -181,4 +181,4 @@ sweet_entitlements_copy_object(const void *obj, const char *name)
 	return v;
 }
 }
-#endif /* SWEET */
+#endif /* SWEET || MILANF */
